    <introduction><p>Let <m>X = \{n \in \N \st 0 \le n \le 999\}</m> be the set of all numbers with three or fewer digits. Define the function <m>f:X \to \N</m> by <m>f(abc) = a+b+c\text{,}</m> where <m>a\text{,}</m> <m>b\text{,}</m> and <m>c</m> are the digits of the number in <m>X</m> (write numbers less than 100 with leading 0<rsq/>s to make them three digits). In other words, <m>f</m> returns the sum of the digits of its input. For example, <m>f(253) = 2 + 5 + 3 =  10\text{.}</m></p>
</introduction>
    <task>
      <statement><p>Let <m>A = \{n \in X \st 309 \le x \le 326\}\text{.}</m>  Find <m>f(A)\text{.}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
